  "存在否定及否定变化，具体用法见正文": "Negative existence and negative change of state; see the text for usage",
  "否定谓词的不规则词形": "Irregular forms of negative predicates",
  "合音与韵母变化": "Contraction and rime changes",
  "表示未然态的i可以与前一音节的韵部结合，引起韵母变化。": "Irrealis i can combine with the preceding syllable’s rime, changing its form.",
  "逐词：吃｜未然态": "Gloss: eat | IRR",
  "常见的不规则词形": "Common irregular forms",
  "xiao、enzou分别是xie“有”、enzi“来”的完成形式。两者都使用缩合后的词形；*xiebolu、*xieliao、*enziliao、*enzibolu不合用法。星号表示不接受的形式。tai、tao也属于不规则词形。": "xiao and enzou are the completed forms of xie ‘have’ and enzi ‘come’. Both require contraction: *xiebolu, *xieliao, *enziliao and *enzibolu are unacceptable. An asterisk marks an unacceptable form. tai and tao also have irregular forms.",
  "“去／去了”“来／来了”的配对及使用限制见未刊补充材料。各词读音可参照 Brassett 词库：hxif“go”（词条949；STEDT rn 456438、454319），zaor“gone”（rn 458308、453837、454441），enrzir“come!”（词条683；rn 456136、454303），enrzouf“come”（rn 456121）。英语词表采用另一套调类编号，此处已换算为叶氏拼音。IPA按Brassett调类1/2/3/4→55/24/21/51及拼写音值映射得到。词库提供读音记录；上述配对与使用限制尚无公开文献出处。": "The pairings ‘go / have gone’ and ‘come / have come’, and their usage restrictions, come from unpublished supplementary material. Pronunciations can be compared with the Brassett lexicon: hxif ‘go’ (entry 949; STEDT rn 456438, 454319), zaor ‘gone’ (rn 458308, 453837, 454441), enrzir ‘come!’ (entry 683; rn 456136, 454303) and enrzouf ‘come’ (rn 456121). The English wordlist uses a different tone-numbering system, converted here to Ye spelling. IPA follows the Brassett mapping of tone classes 1/2/3/4 to 55/24/21/51 and the corresponding segment values. The lexicon supplies pronunciation records; no published source has yet been identified for these pairings and usage restrictions.",
  "谓语用法与修饰、指称形式": "Predicative, modifying and referential forms",
  "“好、长、大”等词作谓语时用基本形式，修饰名词或指称“好的那个、长的那个”时可使用另一种词形。后者既能作定语，也能独立指称事物。": "Words such as ‘good’, ‘long’ and ‘large’ use their basic forms as predicates, but may take a different form when modifying a noun or referring to ‘the good one’ or ‘the long one’. These forms can both modify nouns and refer to things independently.",
  "谓语形式（拼音／IPA）": "Predicate form (romanization / IPA)",
  "修饰、指称形式（拼音／IPA）": "Modifying or referential form (romanization / IPA)",
  "变化特点": "Type of change",
  "好 → 好的": "Good → the good one",
  "韵母变化": "Rime change",
  "长 → 长的": "Long → the long one",
  "后接bar": "Addition of bar",
  "大 → 大的": "Large → the large one",
  "增加成分，并有声调变化": "An added element and a tone change",
  "出处：Brassett等（2006），第100页，表6.1；“好、长”的短语例见第101页例66、69、71、72。这些变化属于特定词的固定词形。没有专门词形的性质词可使用ɲie ɕi名词化结构；颜色词则可不改变词形，用于谓语和修饰语。": "Source: Brassett et al. (2006), p. 100, Table 6.1; phrases with ‘good’ and ‘long’ are on p. 101, examples 66, 69, 71 and 72. These are fixed forms of particular words. Property words without a special form can use the ɲie ɕi nominalization construction. Colour words can retain the same form as predicates and modifiers.",
  "下面的“好的”既能修饰“人”，也能独立指称所取的东西。": "In the following examples, ‘good’ in its referential form both modifies ‘person’ and independently refers to the thing being taken.",
  "性质修饰语常放在中心名词后、数量组前。": "Property modifiers usually follow the head noun and precede the quantity phrase.",
  "性质词的名词化": "Nominalization of property words",
  "有些性质词通过名词化标记组成修饰语；下例在“脏”后加 /ɲie²¹ ɕi²⁴/，修饰前面的“碗”。": "Some property words form modifiers through nominalization. The example below adds /ɲie²¹ ɕi²⁴/ to ‘dirty’ to modify the preceding ‘bowl’.",
  "状态变化见": "For changes of state, see",
  "未然态、预期体与起始体": "Irrealis, prospective and inchoative",
  "；状态的否定见": "; for negation of states, see",
  "禁止、停止与状态不再持续": "Prohibition, stopping and states that no longer hold",
  "感受评价与难易评价": "Sensory evaluation and ease of action",
  "评价动作做得怎样，如“吃得好、地耕得好”，见": "For evaluations of how well an action is performed, such as ‘eat well’ or ‘plough the field well’, see",
  "xi的动作评价用法": "Evaluating actions with xi",
  "性质词的重叠": "Reduplication of property words",
  "性质词重叠可以加强程度。还有在两次重复之间加入 /lie²¹/ 的形式。": "Reduplication can intensify a property. Another pattern places /lie²¹/ between two copies of the word.",
  "固定的程度形式": "Fixed degree expressions",
  "有些程度表达是特定词的固定搭配，主要用作谓语。例如，下面“很好”的形式是“好＋/ti⁵⁵/＋好＋/ka²⁴/”。": "Some degree expressions are fixed combinations with particular words and mainly function as predicates. For example, the form meaning ‘very good’ below consists of ‘good + /ti⁵⁵/ + good + /ka²⁴/’.",
  "动作与状态的程度表达": "Degree expressions with actions and states",
  "冷死了（冷＋死＋了）。": "Freezing cold (literally ‘cold + die + completion marker’).",
  "性质词后加xi，再接tai“没有”，也可加强程度，如“今天好冷”。例句与分析见": "Adding xi and then tai ‘not exist’ to a property word can also express high degree, as in ‘It is so cold today’. For examples and analysis, see",
  "比较基准与差量": "Standard of comparison and degree of difference",
  "结构：比较基准〔话题〕＋被比较者＋（程度量）＋性质谓词＋niex": "Structure: standard of comparison [topic] + entity being compared + (degree of difference) + property predicate + niex",
  "数量限制": "Quantity restrictions",
  "这一限制构式由数量短语、动词和 /ɕi²¹ səu³⁵/ 组成；/ɕi²¹ səu³⁵/ 整体表示“只／仅限”。": "This restrictive construction consists of a quantity phrase, a verb and /ɕi²¹ səu³⁵/. The whole sequence /ɕi²¹ səu³⁵/ means ‘only / limited to’.",
  "完整体把动作作为整体来陈述，完结体突出过程达到终点，完成体突出已发生的动作与当下的联系。": "Perfective aspect presents an action as a whole; completive aspect highlights reaching an endpoint; perfect aspect links a prior action to the present.",
