Object.assign(UI_TRANSLATIONS,{
  "人称代词区分第一、第二、第三人称和单复数；人称代词不分性别。第一、第三人称复数在日常口语中有缩略式。": "Personal pronouns distinguish first, second and third person, and singular and plural. Personal pronouns do not distinguish gender. First- and third-person plurals have shortened forms in everyday speech.",
  "指示代词与距离": "Demonstratives and distance",
  "指示代词可以独立指称人或事物，也可以放在名词前作修饰语。北部材料中的“这”和“那”各有多种形式；Brassett 的 gerdix、aixdix 是其中一组，同一形式可用于单数或复数。": "Demonstratives can independently refer to people or things, or precede a noun as a modifier. Northern sources record several forms for both ‘this’ and ‘that’. Brassett’s gerdix and aixdix are one such pair, with the same forms used for singular and plural reference.",
  "指人、指物的形式": "Forms referring to people and things",
  "形式（IPA）": "Form (IPA)",
  "词库记录": "Lexicon record",
  "这、这个": "This; this one",
  "Brassett 词库，": "Brassett lexicon,",
  "词条733": "entry 733",
  "词条666": "entry 666",
  "这": "this",
  "那、那个": "That; that one",
  "那": "that",
  "词条1584": "entry 1584",
  "这些记录包括不同来源的音形和长短形式。词库中同译为“这”或“那”的词，具体使用范围还要结合调查点和句子判断。": "These records include different source pronunciations and both short and longer forms. The distribution of words glossed as ‘this’ or ‘that’ needs to be considered in relation to the locality and sentence in which they occur.",
  "处所形式与距离等级": "Locative forms and degrees of distance",
  "“这里／那里”有相应的处所形式。例如 /kɤ²¹tu⁵⁵/、/ɜŋ⁵⁵tu⁵⁵/ 表示“这里”，/ai⁵⁵tu⁵⁵/、/au⁵⁵tu⁵⁵/ 表示“那里”；/a²⁴kɤ⁵⁵/ 在词库中释为较远的“那里”。": "Corresponding locative forms express ‘here’ and ‘there’. For example, /kɤ²¹tu⁵⁵/ and /ɜŋ⁵⁵tu⁵⁵/ mean ‘here’, while /ai⁵⁵tu⁵⁵/ and /au⁵⁵tu⁵⁵/ mean ‘there’. The lexicon glosses /a²⁴kɤ⁵⁵/ as ‘there (far away)’.",
  "出处：Brassett 词库，": "Source: Brassett lexicon,",
  "词条739": "entry 739",
  "《土家语简志》把处所指示词分为五个距离等级：近指、较近指、远指、较远指、更远指。最远处还可用远指形式重叠并加重音来表达。因此，处所指示的距离区别比简单的“这／那”更细。": "A Brief Description of Tujia distinguishes five degrees of distance in locative demonstratives: near, relatively near, distant, farther and farthest. The farthest location can also be expressed by reduplicating a distal form and adding stress. Locative demonstratives thus make finer distinctions than a simple ‘this / that’ contrast.",
  "出处：田德生、何天贞等《土家语简志》（1986），第52—53页，": "Source: Tian Desheng, He Tianzhen et al., A Brief Description of Tujia (1986), pp. 52–53,",
  "原书": "original publication",
  "不同文献划分的范围也有差别：陈康《土家语研究》在人、物、时间及方式等用法下列近指和远指；《土家语简志》的五级划分专指处所。把它们同近指、中指、远指的三分法比较时，需要先看所指的是人、物还是地点。": "The classifications also differ in scope. Chen Kang’s A Study of Tujia lists proximal and distal forms for people, things, time and manner, while the five-way distinction in A Brief Description of Tujia specifically concerns locations. Comparison with a proximal–medial–distal system therefore requires attention to whether the referent is a person, a thing or a place.",
  "出处：陈康《土家语研究》（2006），第62—63页，": "Source: Chen Kang, A Study of Tujia (2006), pp. 62–63,",
  "；田德生、何天贞等《土家语简志》（1986），第52—54页。": "; Tian Desheng, He Tianzhen et al., A Brief Description of Tujia (1986), pp. 52–54.",
  "Brassett等，第137–139页，例204、208–209及213–217，分别对比行动迫近、计划中的行动与过程开始。补充口语例句见“吃中饭”的未刊补充语料注。": "Brassett et al., pp. 137–139, examples 204, 208–209 and 213–217, contrast imminent action, planned action and the onset of a process. For the supplementary spoken examples, see the note on the unpublished ‘eat lunch’ data.",
  "这类表达可按“［动词＋处所名词化］＋有／没有”分析：“没有”否定的是可供活动的地方。Brassett 也把相应的 /tsuɔ²¹/ 单列为处所名词化标记。": "These expressions have the structure ‘[verb + place nominalizer] + exist / not exist’. The negative denies the availability of a place for the activity. Brassett likewise lists the corresponding /tsuɔ²¹/ as a place nominalizer.",
  "Brassett等（2006），第141—142页，§8.1；田志慧，第541页。": "Brassett et al. (2006), pp. 141–142, §8.1; Tian Zhihui, p. 541."
});
